+\subsubsection{Configuration-resolved spectroscopic response and generalized King diagnostics}
+\label{subsubsec:rt_configuration_resolved_spectroscopic_response}
+\paragraph{Status.}
+\textbf{[RESEARCH-TRACK / LINEAR-RESPONSE STRUCTURE DEFINED / ATOMIC ENERGY
+FUNCTIONAL AND SELECTION RULES OPEN].}
+The purpose of this subsection is to connect the canonical mass and topology
+functionals to precision-spectroscopy diagnostics without claiming that SST
+already derives an atomic spectrum.  The neutral-ytterbium inner-shell clock
+programme provides a useful methodological template because several transition
+channels and isotope pairs are used to expose departures from a low-rank
+factorization model \cite{IshiyamaEtAl2026Yb431}.
+
+For an SST configuration $K$, define
+\begin{align}
+    \Delta E_i^{(K)}
+    &\equiv
+    E_{i,e}^{(K)}-E_{i,g}^{(K)},
+    &
+    \nu_i^{(K)}
+    &\equiv
+    \frac{\Delta E_i^{(K)}}{h}.
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_transition_energy_def}
+\end{align}
+Let $q_A^{(K)}$ be a preregistered set of independent configuration variables.
+The first-order response is
+\begin{align}
+    \delta\nu_i^{(K)}
+    &=
+    \frac{1}{h}
+    \sum_A
+    \frac{\partial\Delta E_i^{(K)}}{\partial q_A^{(K)}}
+    \,\delta q_A^{(K)}
+    +O(\delta q^2).
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_spectroscopic_linear_response}
+\end{align}
+A compact admissible basis is
+\begin{align}
+    q_A^{(K)}
+    \in
+    \left\{
+        M_K,
+        I_{K,ab},
+        \Xi_K,
+        \SwirlClock,
+        \ldots
+    \right\},
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_response_compact_basis}
+\end{align}
+where $I_{K,ab}$ is a configuration-dependent inertia tensor.  In this basis,
+$M_K$ carries the scalar rest-energy scale while $I_{K,ab}$ carries orientation-
+and anisotropy-sensitive response.  No scalar moment of inertia is presumed
+sufficient for an anisotropic transition.
+
+A resolved geometric basis may instead be used:
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal Q_K
+    \equiv
+    \left(
+        C_K,
+        L_K,
+        \mathcal H_K,
+        k_K,
+        \Lambda_K^{\rm strut},
+        \Lambda_K^{\rm kink},
+        \SwirlClock
+    \right),
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_response_resolved_basis}
+\end{align}
+with
+\begin{align}
+    \Lambda_K^{\rm strut}
+    &\equiv
+    \sum_{(p,q)\in\operatorname{Strut}(K)}\lambda_{pq},
+    &
+    \Lambda_K^{\rm kink}
+    &\equiv
+    \sum_{j\in\operatorname{Kink}(K)}\mu_j.
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_contact_response_sums}
+\end{align}
+The corresponding response can be written schematically as
+\begin{align}
+    \delta\nu_i^{(K)}
+    =
+    \frac{1}{h}
+    \left[
+        \frac{\partial\Delta E_i}{\partial M_K}\,\delta M_K
+        +
+        \frac{\partial\Delta E_i}{\partial I_{K,ab}}\,\delta I_{K,ab}
+        +
+        \sum_\mu
+        \frac{\partial\Delta E_i}{\partial \mathcal Q_{K,\mu}}
+        \,\delta\mathcal Q_{K,\mu}
+    \right]
+    +O(\delta q^2).
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_spectroscopic_resolved_response}
+\end{align}
+Repeated Cartesian indices are summed.  The response coefficients in
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_configuration_spectroscopic_resolved_response} are derivatives
+of one shared transition-energy functional; they are not independent free
+coefficients to be assigned separately for every line.
+
+\paragraph{Kernel-dependency guard.}
+For the canonical kernel
+\begin{align}
+    \Xi_K
+    =
+    \left[
+        \alpha_C C_K+
+        \beta_L L_K+
+        \gamma_H\mathcal H_K
+    \right]\varphi^{-2k_K},
+\end{align}
+its variation is
+\begin{align}
+    \delta\Xi_K
+    =
+    \varphi^{-2k_K}
+    \left(
+        \alpha_C\,\delta C_K+
+        \beta_L\,\delta L_K+
+        \gamma_H\,\delta\mathcal H_K
+    \right)
+    -2\ln\varphi\,\Xi_K\,\delta k_K,
+    \label{eq:rt_configuration_kernel_variation}
+\end{align}
+when the matching coefficients are held fixed.  Therefore
+$\delta\mathcal H_K$ and $\delta\Xi_K$ are not independent directions in the
+same fit.  A calculation must choose either the compact basis
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_configuration_response_compact_basis} or the resolved basis
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_configuration_response_resolved_basis}, unless an explicit
+Jacobian, projection, or orthogonalization removes the redundancy.
+
+\paragraph{Generalized King diagnostic.}
+For isotope pairs $A',A$, a spectroscopy model may be organized as
+\begin{align}
+    \delta\nu_i^{A'A}
+    =
+    K_i w^{A'A}
+    +F_i\,\delta\!\left\langle r^2\right\rangle^{A'A}
+    +\sum_\mu S_{i\mu}\,\delta\mathcal Q_\mu^{A'A},
+    \label{eq:rt_sst_generalized_king_diagnostic}
+\end{align}
+where
+\begin{align}
+    \delta\mathcal Q_\mu^{A'A}
+    \equiv
+    \mathcal Q_\mu^{A'}-\mathcal Q_\mu^A.
+\end{align}
+Equation~\eqref{eq:rt_sst_generalized_king_diagnostic} is a diagnostic
+factorization, not a derived SST isotope-shift law.  A nonlinear residual means
+first that the selected low-rank basis is incomplete.  It identifies an SST
+sector only if the same preregistered $\mathcal Q_\mu$ and shared response
+functional explain multiple independent transitions and isotope pairs without
+line-by-line refitting.
+
+\paragraph{Certification gates.}
+Promotion requires all of the following:
+\begin{enumerate}
+    \item $E_{i,g}^{(K)}$ and $E_{i,e}^{(K)}$ follow from one declared SST
+    energy functional and one boundary-condition class;
+    \item the response coefficients are derivatives of that shared functional,
+    not independent parameters for each transition;
+    \item $M_K$, $\Xi_K$, $\mathcal H_K$, and contact variables are counted in
+    an explicitly independent coordinate basis;
+    \item the same configuration variables describe at least three independent
+    transition channels and more isotope pairs than free nuclear/configuration
+    directions;
+    \item selection rules and state labels are derived dynamically rather than
+    imported solely from the measured spectrum;
+    \item at least one withheld transition or isotope pair is predicted outside
+    the calibration set;
+    \item residuals are stable under numerical resolution, admissible core
+    profiles, contact-map perturbations, and uncertainty propagation.
+\end{enumerate}
+Failure of any gate blocks promotion.  In particular, high-significance King
+nonlinearity alone is not evidence for SST ontology, just as it is not by itself
+proof of a new mediator.
+
